(
 '* 5.0.3 ⋄ 2026-10-02'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * `SetTrap` with an empty right argument produced a `⎕TRAP` pointing to a non-existing function'
 '      when HandleError was loaded as a Tatin package. It also assumed the namespace to be called `HandleError`'
 '    * SaveVisibleVars did not reach through to the namespace where the actual crash happened'
 '    * A failure in SaveVisibleVars made Process give up silently'
 '    * Process destroyed the crash namespace in case SaveErrorWorkspace failed; as a side effect'
 '      nothing was written to the Windows Event Log'
 '    * If collecting the crash information failed, Process skipped everything else, including `⎕OFF`'
 '    * The name of a parameter space that does not exist (any more) made Process give up silently;'
 '      it now carries on with the defaults'
 '    * The parameter `trapInternalErrors` had no effect in Process'
 '    * In case SaveErrorWorkspace failed it did not report the real reason'
 '    * `⎕TRAP`, `⎕IO` and `⎕ML` were not reported correctly; `⎕WA` and `⎕TNUMS` were taken after'
 '      the threads had been killed'
 '    * Several pieces of textual information should have been HTML-escaped but weren''t'
 '    * CheckErrorFolder did set `⎕WSID` but did not reset it'
 '    * Two crashes in the same second collided because CreateFilename did not use milliseconds'
 '  * `SetTrap` rejects a reference with a clear message: it requires the name of a namespace'
 '  * The stack reported in `crash` and the HTML page no longer contains HandleError''s own functions'
 '  * In a `CLEAR WS` crash files now go into `%LOCALAPPDATA%/ERROR_WS/Errors` (Windows) rather than'
 '    `%LOCALAPPDATA%/CLEAR WS/Errors`'
 '  * `WindowsEventLog` (and with it `OS`) is no longer a dependency of the package: only the tests need it'
 '  * CheckErrorFolder no longer starts `cmd.exe` (Windows) or a shell (Linux/macOS)'
 '  * The parameter `trapSaveWSID` is deprecated and ignored: `trapInternalErrors` now governs saving the error WS as well'
 '  * Documentation corrected and improved'
 '* 5.0.2 ⋄ 2025-07-18'
 '  * Serious bug in `SetTrap` fixed: did address the `Process` incorrectly when loaded as a package'
 '* 5.0.1 ⋄ 2025-07-17'
 '  * The documentation on `ADOC_Doc` was flawed.  '
 '* 5.0.0 ⋄ 2025-04-08'
 '  * Class converted to an ordinary namespace'
 '  * `Version` now returns just a char vector with the version info from the package config file (potentially breaking)'
 '  * `Message` is now added to the error message at the bottom of the HTML report, and removed from the top. (#4)      '
 '  * Packages updated'
 '  * `Make` improved'
 '* 4.1.4 ⋄ 2023-04-18'
 '  * Bug fix: the structure of the project was wrong, resulting in test-related stuff being included'
 '    in the package: that caused the naming problem.'
 '* 4.1.3 ⋄ 2023-04-17'
 '  * All functions with a "∆" in their names removed from the project: the Mac-OS can''t stand them'
 '    Otherwise the software is unchanged.'
 '* 4.1.2 ⋄ 2023-04-10'
 '  * ⎕TNUMS was reported in too many cells'
 '* 4.1.1 ⋄ 2021-07-24'
 '  * `Process` now uses `:Hold` for preventing itself from running twice in two threads.'
 '  * Documentation polished'
 '  * Dependencies updated'
 '  * "Make" now uses the `MakeHelpers` package and is called by the newly introduced `Admin.Make` function'
 '* 4.1.0'
 '  * Parameter `killThreads` introduced.'
 '  * `Process` hardened against unforseeable problems.'
 '  * Bug fix: `Process` executed either `⎕OFF` or `→`; in the latter case it shouldn''t.'
 '* 4.0.2'
 '  * Package config file corrected'
 '* 4.0.1'
 '  * Documentation improved'
 '  * Tests polished'
 '* 4.0.0'
 '  * BREAKING CHANGES:'
 '    * Requires at least Dyalog 18.0'
 '    * Requires the class `APLTreeUtils2`'
 '  * Does not `:Include APLTreeUtils` anymore'
 '  * Bug fixes:'
 '    * Empty `⎕WSID` (stand-alone-EXE!) can cause havoc (#1)'
 '    * `Process` does not return the name of the error workspace because the function either'
 '      executed `⎕OFF` or `→`. The name is now assigned to `∆ERROR_WS` in the parameter space.'
 ''
 'For information regarding older versions see <https://github.com/aplteam/HandleError/releases>'
 ''
)
